course: dictionary
lesson: 8327
title: Which meaning fits? Clues from context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. Roe is one of these words. «Cod roe» and «roe deer» both use roe, but they mean very different things.
explain: Look at the nearby words. If the text talks about fish, eating or eggs, roe means the eggs inside a female fish. If it talks about deer, woods or a coat, roe means a small deer. In «Roe deer are small, about 70 centimetres at the shoulder», the word deer tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. «The roe was small and had a reddish coat» makes sense for the deer, but not for the fish eggs. If your meaning does not fit, try the other one.
fact: Roe means the mass of eggs inside a female fish, often eaten as food.
fact: A roe, or roe deer, is a small deer of Europe and Asia with a reddish coat.
fact: The male roe deer is called a roebuck.
fact: «Cod roe» and «salmon roe» are eaten in many countries, and caviar is the roe of the sturgeon.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, roe deer live in woods.
exercise: «Cod roe» is eaten in many countries. What is cod roe? | A kind of fish bone | A type of bread | A small deer | *The eggs inside a female cod
exercise: «Roe deer are small, about 70 centimetres at the shoulder.» What is a roe in this sentence? | A bird | A farm animal | Fish eggs | *A small deer
exercise: «The roebuck stood still in the wood.» What is a roebuck? | A female fish | A small grey bird | *The male roe deer | A type of fishing net
test: «Scientists watched the roe develop in the water.» What does roe mean here? | *Fish eggs | A young fox | A small deer | A kind of green plant
test: Which two kinds of deer living wild in Britain are native, not brought by people? | Fallow and Chinese water deer | *Red and roe | Muntjac and sika | Red and fallow
exam: Caviar is the roe of which fish? | Trout | Salmon | *Sturgeon | Cod
